From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mohamed Ahmed <mohamedahmedegypt2001@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 19:44:08 +0400
Subject: drm/nouveau/dispnv50: validate and program output scaling

Nouveau programs viewport sizes without checking whether the output
scaler can support the resulting ratio. On Turing and later, reject modes
beyond the postcomp viewport limit at probe and unsupported scaling
ratios at atomic check. The dimension limit is 16384 on GB20x and 8192 on
earlier classes.

Select taps from the scaler capabilities, then program the taps and usage
bounds with the validated viewport. Load the five-tap coefficients at
core init so they are available when a modeset needs them. Reset viewport
offsets on modesets because firmware may have left them nonzero.

On GB20x, enable the RGB2ITP and ITP2RGB FVLUTs while scaling. The
postcomp scaler requires fixed-point samples between these blocks and
otherwise misinterprets FP16 data.

Scaling and underscan changes alter the viewport used for mode
validation, so require a full modeset to validate the new configuration.

Signed-off-by: Mohamed Ahmed <mohamedahmedegypt2001@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 2b552e42560f80f81695b4d7cd9348c9998a476c)
